<title>SRI LANKA: Weather-Rain seen over most parts of Sri Lanka.</title>
<headline>Weather-Rain seen over most parts of Sri Lanka.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-05-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's metereological department released the following rainfall figures for 24 hours ending Saturday morning</p>
<p>Hydro catchment areas (in mm):</p>
<p>    Canyon		    5.5</p>
<p>    Castlereigh	    16.0</p>
<p>    Kotmale		   8.0</p>
<p>    Laxapana		 21.8</p>
<p>    Moussakele	     30.6</p>
<p>    Norton		   14.0</p>
<p>    Randenigala	     0</p>
<p>    Victoria		  0</p>
<p>    Samanalawewa	   39.0</p>
<p>    Ukuwela		  11.2</p>
<p>    Rantembe		  0</p>
<p>The department forecasts thundershowers in most parts of the island during Sunday afternoon or evening. It forecasts occasional thunder showers in deep and shallow sea areas off the eastern and southern coast.</p>
</text>
